# LF in the repository and in every checkout, Windows included.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows'
# default) writes CRLF into every file: the shell scripts stop running under
# bash ($'\r': command not found — build-test.sh itself among them), and the
# tests that compare generated copies byte for byte fail. The server, the Pi
# and the Oracle tower all read these files as LF. See docs/DECISIONS.md
# 2026-10-13.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe misreads labels in LF batch files; these are only ever run on Windows.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touch these, whatever their first bytes look like.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary
*.tar binary
*.gephi binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
